1
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:02,178
Friday night,

2
00:00:02,178 --> 00:00:05,246
you order a 25,000-won fried chicken.

3
00:00:05,246 --> 00:00:08,480
The owner who fried it keeps 3,037 won.

4
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:11,832
Stranger still: chicken shops close every day,

5
00:00:11,832 --> 00:00:14,050
yet the app collecting the fees has seen

6
00:00:14,050 --> 00:00:15,770
profits fall two years running.

7
00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:19,138
Bottom line: the power to split the price sits

8
00:00:19,138 --> 00:00:21,884
with whoever controls the path every order takes,

9
00:00:21,884 --> 00:00:23,566
not whoever fries the chicken.

10
00:00:23,566 --> 00:00:26,480
That's why Uber now wants to buy that path outright.

11
00:00:27,280 --> 00:00:31,715
If neither the owner nor the app is smiling,

12
00:00:31,715 --> 00:00:32,420
who is?

13
00:00:33,230 --> 00:00:35,983
Let's follow this story from a paper flyer all

14
00:00:35,983 --> 00:00:37,480
the way to San Francisco,

15
00:00:37,480 --> 00:00:40,293
and by the end you'll know how to save a little

16
00:00:40,293 --> 00:00:41,550
on tonight's chicken.

17
00:00:43,250 --> 00:00:44,295
Story one, 2010.

18
00:00:44,295 --> 00:00:46,971
A designer-turned-founder began gathering

19
00:00:46,971 --> 00:00:50,170
neighborhood restaurant flyers into a single app.

20
00:00:50,970 --> 00:00:53,203
Smartphones were just spreading.

21
00:00:53,203 --> 00:00:57,040
Flyers stuck on the fridge moved into one phone screen.

22
00:00:57,240 --> 00:01:00,808
People opened the app instead of hunting for numbers,

23
00:01:00,808 --> 00:01:03,770
and restaurants lined up to be listed on it.

24
00:01:04,570 --> 00:01:05,898
Then in late 2019,

25
00:01:05,898 --> 00:01:09,884
Germany's Delivery Hero announced it would buy Baemin,

26
00:01:09,884 --> 00:01:11,950
for about 4.75 trillion won.

27
00:01:12,150 --> 00:01:15,572
A company that neither fried chicken nor delivered it.

28
00:01:15,572 --> 00:01:18,170
The path orders take was worth that much.

29
00:01:18,370 --> 00:01:22,630
Months later, that value was put to the test.

30
00:01:24,330 --> 00:01:27,090
Story two, April 1, 2020.

31
00:01:27,090 --> 00:01:32,059
Baemin switched from a flat monthly ad fee to

32
00:01:32,059 --> 00:01:35,040
taking 5.8% of every order.

33
00:01:35,850 --> 00:01:39,705
Owners already hurt by COVID called it a hidden fee hike.

34
00:01:39,705 --> 00:01:43,222
Customers deleted the app and left one-star reviews,

35
00:01:43,222 --> 00:01:44,980
and politicians joined in.

36
00:01:45,180 --> 00:01:48,987
The FTC was reviewing Delivery Hero's purchase at the time.

37
00:01:48,987 --> 00:01:52,730
Within ten days Baemin apologized and scrapped the change.

38
00:01:53,530 --> 00:01:54,862
But that same year,

39
00:01:54,862 --> 00:01:58,647
something no one expected: with eating out restricted,

40
00:01:58,647 --> 00:02:00,540
people started ordering in.

41
00:02:01,330 --> 00:02:03,476
That year Baemin's revenue topped 1 trillion

42
00:02:03,476 --> 00:02:04,597
won for the first time,

43
00:02:04,597 --> 00:02:06,060
nearly double the year before.

44
00:02:06,260 --> 00:02:09,650
That December the FTC approved the deal,

45
00:02:09,650 --> 00:02:14,990
with one condition that matters again at the end of this story.

46
00:02:15,790 --> 00:02:19,295
In the very year everyone was furious about fees,

47
00:02:19,295 --> 00:02:21,870
the value of the order path went up.

48
00:02:23,570 --> 00:02:28,308
Story three: let's open tonight's chicken bag,

49
00:02:28,308 --> 00:02:34,900
using Asia Economy's breakdown of a 25,000-won chicken in Seoul.

50
00:02:35,710 --> 00:02:38,239
The biggest slice isn't fees. Chicken,

51
00:02:38,239 --> 00:02:42,366
oil and packaging bought through headquarters cost 11,480 won,

52
00:02:42,366 --> 00:02:43,830
nearly half the price.

53
00:02:44,630 --> 00:02:46,746
Next comes the app: commission,

54
00:02:46,746 --> 00:02:49,886
delivery and payment fees add up to 6,710 won,

55
00:02:49,886 --> 00:02:52,480
more than double what the owner keeps.

56
00:02:53,280 --> 00:02:55,764
Say you opened a chicken shop in your

57
00:02:55,764 --> 00:02:58,650
neighborhood and sold 50 a day by delivery.

58
00:02:58,850 --> 00:03:03,812
The app's share alone would top 10 million won a month,

59
00:03:03,812 --> 00:03:06,880
before your own pay and utilities.

60
00:03:07,680 --> 00:03:10,296
Add ads to get listed near the top,

61
00:03:10,296 --> 00:03:15,230
and in the same calculation platform costs reach 40% of the order.

62
00:03:16,020 --> 00:03:20,595
Seoul tracked 186 franchise shops for a year:

63
00:03:20,595 --> 00:03:25,780
fees' share of delivery sales rose from 17% to 24%.

64
00:03:26,590 --> 00:03:28,215
So some can't hold on.

65
00:03:28,215 --> 00:03:32,130
Last year restaurants filed about 390 closures a day.

66
00:03:32,930 --> 00:03:36,640
Here's the twist: closures don't shrink the app's revenue,

67
00:03:36,640 --> 00:03:39,710
because it earns on every order, not every shop.

68
00:03:39,910 --> 00:03:44,031
If shop A closes and its customers order from shop B,

69
00:03:44,031 --> 00:03:45,820
the fee still comes in.

70
00:03:46,620 --> 00:03:50,440
The biggest slice, supplies, hides HQ's cut too.

71
00:03:50,640 --> 00:03:53,524
Chicken HQs made an average 41 million won in

72
00:03:53,524 --> 00:03:55,511
supply markup per shop in 2024,

73
00:03:55,511 --> 00:03:57,690
close to a worker's annual salary.

74
00:03:57,890 --> 00:04:00,774
In January the Supreme Court ordered Pizza Hut

75
00:04:00,774 --> 00:04:04,160
Korea to return markups taken without owners' consent.

76
00:04:05,870 --> 00:04:09,880
Story four: so was the app thrilled? No.

77
00:04:10,680 --> 00:04:13,996
Baemin's operating profit fell two years

78
00:04:13,996 --> 00:04:17,560
running; 2025 was more than 100 billion won

79
00:04:17,560 --> 00:04:19,550
below two years earlier.

80
00:04:20,350 --> 00:04:23,357
In spring 2024 Coupang Eats offered free

81
00:04:23,357 --> 00:04:25,536
delivery and Baemin followed,

82
00:04:25,536 --> 00:04:29,520
both paying delivery costs to win the same customers.

83
00:04:30,320 --> 00:04:33,615
Free delivery doesn't make the cost vanish.

84
00:04:33,615 --> 00:04:35,378
Someone pays the rider,

85
00:04:35,378 --> 00:04:37,524
and as the app took that on,

86
00:04:37,524 --> 00:04:39,670
costs grew with every order.

87
00:04:39,870 --> 00:04:42,621
But retreat wasn't an option: lose the users

88
00:04:42,621 --> 00:04:44,560
and the path itself is at risk.

89
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:47,700
In a market where new users are scarce,

90
00:04:47,700 --> 00:04:49,560
what's the fastest way to grow?

91
00:04:49,560 --> 00:04:51,300
The answer came from America.

92
00:04:52,100 --> 00:04:54,583
America's top delivery app DoorDash bought

93
00:04:54,583 --> 00:04:56,356
Britain's Deliveroo last year,

94
00:04:56,356 --> 00:04:58,897
and last month announced a deal for grocery

95
00:04:58,897 --> 00:05:01,380
delivery app Instacart: growing by buying.

96
00:05:03,080 --> 00:05:04,054
Story five,

97
00:05:04,054 --> 00:05:09,102
last July: Uber made a public offer to buy Delivery Hero,

98
00:05:09,102 --> 00:05:10,430
Baemin's owner.

99
00:05:11,230 --> 00:05:13,340
The deal is worth about 21 trillion won.

100
00:05:13,550 --> 00:05:16,351
The company that bought Baemin for 4.75

101
00:05:16,351 --> 00:05:20,230
trillion won in 2019 is now being bought for far more.

102
00:05:21,030 --> 00:05:22,889
When I worked at a private equity fund,

103
00:05:22,889 --> 00:05:25,082
I developed a data center from the land up and

104
00:05:25,082 --> 00:05:26,750
took part in an AI chip investment.

105
00:05:26,950 --> 00:05:27,848
In every review,

106
00:05:27,848 --> 00:05:31,326
one question was left at the end: if this company disappeared,

107
00:05:31,326 --> 00:05:33,290
could the business route around it?

108
00:05:33,490 --> 00:05:36,917
For a data center that spot is power and fiber; for delivery,

109
00:05:36,917 --> 00:05:39,220
it is the app screen where orders gather.

110
00:05:40,020 --> 00:05:42,540
What Uber is buying isn't chicken; it's that path.

111
00:05:42,740 --> 00:05:43,734
If the deal closes,

112
00:05:43,734 --> 00:05:46,035
fees on chicken fried in Seoul land in a San

113
00:05:46,035 --> 00:05:47,500
Francisco company's results.

114
00:05:47,700 --> 00:05:50,616
In private equity you work out where you will

115
00:05:50,616 --> 00:05:54,051
earn back the price as carefully as the price itself.

116
00:05:54,051 --> 00:05:57,096
That's why owners wonder what a 21-trillion-won

117
00:05:57,096 --> 00:05:59,170
buyer will collect on this path.

118
00:05:59,970 --> 00:06:02,909
Someone does guard that path.

119
00:06:02,909 --> 00:06:07,369
In 2020 the FTC let Delivery Hero buy Baemin

120
00:06:07,369 --> 00:06:09,700
only if it sold Yogiyo.

121
00:06:09,900 --> 00:06:12,904
Putting No.1 and No.2 under one roof would

122
00:06:12,904 --> 00:06:15,837
leave owners and customers nowhere to go.

123
00:06:15,837 --> 00:06:18,913
This September the FTC opened a new review,

124
00:06:18,913 --> 00:06:22,490
and its verdict will decide the path's next owner.

125
00:06:23,280 --> 00:06:26,908
A bill in the National Assembly would cap total fees,

126
00:06:26,908 --> 00:06:29,920
including payment, delivery and ads, at 15%.

127
00:06:30,130 --> 00:06:32,542
Critics say a cap could cut free-delivery

128
00:06:32,542 --> 00:06:35,600
support and push delivery costs back onto customers.

129
00:06:36,400 --> 00:06:39,360
One more thing for those who stayed: on ValueNote,

130
00:06:39,360 --> 00:06:41,668
which scores companies by the standards

131
00:06:41,668 --> 00:06:43,681
investors like Warren Buffett use,

132
00:06:43,681 --> 00:06:45,220
Uber scores 39 out of 100.

133
00:06:45,420 --> 00:06:46,759
If Baemin changes hands,

134
00:06:46,759 --> 00:06:49,159
tonight's chicken orders become part of the

135
00:06:49,159 --> 00:06:50,610
numbers behind that score.

136
00:06:51,410 --> 00:06:56,952
In one line: the power to split the price lies in the order path,

137
00:06:56,952 --> 00:07:00,960
and the fight over who owns it has gone global.

138
00:07:01,160 --> 00:07:03,895
It isn't just chicken: lodging apps and

139
00:07:03,895 --> 00:07:06,490
ride-hailing apps hold the same spot.

140
00:07:07,290 --> 00:07:09,507
So before you tap order next time,

141
00:07:09,507 --> 00:07:12,310
compare the app price with the shop's menu.

142
00:07:12,310 --> 00:07:15,570
Seven in ten franchises charged more for delivery.

143
00:07:15,770 --> 00:07:19,050
If it's walkable, call and pick it up yourself.

144
00:07:19,050 --> 00:07:22,260
A bit more stays with the owner, and with you.

145
